{:title
 "Label in the Smile Prompt Language, Where a Prompt Meta-Informs a Model While It Instructs",
 :description
 "What a label is in THE MAP of Smile, the words between the faces of a header, with kinds such as name, nesting, lens, origin, author and date, and how my words reached that meaning, from semantic labelling in May 2025 to labels with their own header, body and footer in August 2026, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "prompt labels, semantic labeling, meta information in prompts, origin label, header label, Smile prompt language, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, a label is the text between the start face and the end face of a header or footer line. It is the one place in a line where a prompt meta-informs a model while it instructs.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP gives a label three regions of its own, so several kinds sit in one label in a settled order. Its kinds are name, nesting, lens, origin, author, kind, importance, behaviour, application, date, duration, relation and strictness. Almost all of them are already known when a composition gathers, depth from the walk, author from the card, date from the rings, so labels are drawn from the lens at compose time. Origin is the one that lets a model meet what truly arrived, since text in the position where a person speaks is otherwise read as a person speaking now. Every kind spends context, so how many are shown is graded by the meta-information dimension of [[t:the-two-dimensions]]."
 "A seed of it is on a recording of 28 May 2025, before the faces had their name, where semantic labelling meant any mark that signals a change of meaning. “Semantic labeling is when you use any grammatical symbols or punctuation or even code words. to signal when there's a change in the semantic content of the text”, and the reason it matters, “the meta idea is the most important where it's like you're coining what things are so that you can point them out.”[[m:2025-05-28]]"
 "In the documents of July 2025 a label was a name wrapped in its own marks. The language guidelines of 5 July wrote “When I want to provide a special label for something, I also wrap it like this”,[[m:2025-07-05]] the De-GPT document gave labels their square brackets,[[m:2025-07-08]] and Smile v0.2 used them to speak to the reader of the document itself, “At a meta-level, for this document I use these special labels to talk to any large language models reading this.”[[m:2025-07-10]] The name tag, a label of its own kind, is followed in [[t:semantic-markdown]]."
 "From late 2025 into 2026 labelling became the way a prompt describes itself so a model can use it. On a recording of December, “so what i've done with smile is that every single little bit of prompt text you're also going to describe what it does”, and “on the back end, it's all interpretable because it's all labeled and described.”[[m:2025-12-03]] In February 2026, “now that my things are going to be accurate labels of what things are”, the AI could put prompts together itself.[[m:2026-02-13]] In March I wrote of modules that are labelled and “modular and precise and referring to units and connections between units”.[[m:2026-03-14]] On 31 July 2026 the label was named as the place a prompt meta-informs while it instructs, “where every part of the prompt contains its meta-information about its ontology and the hierarchy”.[[m:2026-07-31]]"
 "In August 2026 the label took the form THE MAP keeps. On 4 August, “The label will also have a header, body, footer.”[[m:2026-08-04]] On 8 August the name of a module was to be carried into the labels of its headers, “basically giving it multiple forms.”[[m:2026-08-08]] On 10 August, “The label of a header can also have a header / body / footer though. as can the smiles.”[[m:2026-08-10]] On 11 August I gave the reason for the kinds, “I want all the models informed of what is actually happening all the time. At the moment if somebody copy pastes, or automates a prompt, the model receives it as a human.”, and named the list as it grew, “nesting label, lens label, origin label, author label”, with “call that date label not currency.”[[m:2026-08-11]] On 15 August a header could have no label at all, “Yeah its just a header with no label.”[[m:2026-08-15]] and on 16 August the label was how “we can add many metadata labels etc and additional informations”.[[m:2026-08-16]]"
 "So the label moved from punctuation that signals a change of meaning in May 2025, through names wrapped in brackets and prompts that describe themselves, to the region of every header where THE MAP has a model told what a piece is, where it came from and who wrote it, still part built, across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes from {{first}} to {{last}}. The piece a label names is followed in [[t:module]]."],
 :faq
 [["What is a label in Smile?"
 "The text between the start face and the end face of a header or footer line, the place where a prompt tells a model what a piece is while it instructs."]
 ["What kinds of label does Smile have?"
 "Name, nesting, lens, origin, author, kind, importance, behaviour, application, date, duration, relation and strictness, drawn from the lens when a composition is gathered."]
 ["Why does Smile have an origin label?"
 "Text placed where a person speaks is read as a person speaking now. The origin label tells a model whether words were typed, pasted or sent by an automation, so it meets what actually arrived."]]}
